  "Plants cannot run away from danger, but that does not mean they simply wait to be eaten. Over the past few decades, biologists have learned that many plants respond to attacks by producing bitter chemicals that make their leaves less tasty. A newer and more surprising question is whether some plants can detect an attack before it reaches them — not by smell or touch, but by sound.",
